# Accessibility

Scope: any UI component or page. Complements the design system in `.cursor/rules/ui-design-system.mdc`.

## Requirements

- **Contrast:** meet WCAG AA (4.5:1 for normal text). Use design tokens; gold text on light must use `--color-accent-button`, not `--color-accent`.
- **Focus:** every interactive element has a visible focus indicator (`focus-visible:ring-2 ring-[var(--color-accent)] ring-offset-2 outline-none` or the `.focus-ring` class).
- **Touch targets:** `min-h-[44px]` (and adequate width) on interactive elements.
- **Names:** `aria-label` on icon-only controls; `aria-hidden="true"` on decorative icons; label all form inputs (`<label htmlFor>` or `aria-label`).
- **Semantics:** use native elements (`button`, `a`, `nav`, headings in order). Only add ARIA roles when a native element can't do the job.
- **Keyboard:** all actions reachable and operable by keyboard; manage focus in modals/drawers; provide skip-to-content where relevant.
- **Reduced motion:** gate animations behind `useReducedMotion()`; provide static fallbacks.
- **Live regions:** use polite live regions for async status/toasts.

## Verification (do not claim a11y without evidence)

- Prefer an automated pass: the repo has `@axe-core/playwright` and `npm run test:e2e:a11y` (`playwright.ci-a11y.config.ts`). Run it for changed pages when feasible.
- For manual checks, use the `accessibility-auditing` skill (keyboard traversal + contrast + screen-reader names) and capture findings.

## Common failure modes

- Adding global `transition-*` on `a, button, [role="button"]` — this breaks Framer Motion site-wide. Never do it.
- Removing focus outlines for aesthetics.
- Placeholder-as-label (no accessible name).
- Color as the only signal for state.
